# Same bytes on every system: text files are stored and checked out with LF, except Windows batch files (the
# launcher), which cmd.exe reads best with CRLF. build_release.py takes files through these rules (its CRLF_SUFFIXES
# match the two lines below), so the release zip is identical whether it is built on Windows or Linux.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.zip binary
*.ba2 binary
*.esm binary
*.esp binary
*.esl binary
# Shared test sets (tools/pmt/shared-tests): a byte-for-byte copy, never changed by line-ending rules.
tests/shared/** -text
